OL,3,GNEWSAWhat should residents worried
OL,4,Aabout cancer-causing forever chemicals
OL,5,Ado?
OL,6,
OL,7,FA public health director is warning
OL,8,Fdozens of people living near a chemical
OL,9,Ffactory who have been found to have
OL,10,F"really high levels" of a potentially
OL,11,Fcancer-causing forever chemical in
OL,12,Ftheir blood to be "really cautious"
OL,13,Fabout the way they interpret their
OL,14,Fblood test results.
OL,16,FSome 49 residents near the AGC
OL,17,FChemicals plant in Thornton-Cleveleys
OL,18,Fwhere PFOA - an industrial substance
OL,19,Fwhich was historically used- were
OL,20,Ftested. Seven out of ten residents were
OL,21,Ffound to have elevated levels.
OL,23,APub: 24-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,404,400,260,160,0,100
